    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Filter Extremes\r\n\r\nUse `notnull()` to limit the analysis to superheroes who have values for both `Affiliation` and `YearsActive`.\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 1]\r\nRun the program. Examine the superheroes with the highest and lowest `PowerLevel` values.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 2]\r\nFilter `strongest_hero` to keep only superheroes who have an `Affiliation`. Then apply another filter to keep only superheroes who have a `YearsActive` value.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 3]\r\nApply the same two `notnull()` filters to `weakest_hero`.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 4]\r\nRun the program and compare the results. How did requiring values in both columns change which superheroes remained?\r\n:::",
    "ai_tutor_available": "false",
    "submittable": "false",
    "hide_share_and_remix": "false",
